{"url": "https://www.uwa.edu.au/projects/data-science-at-uwa", "final_url": "https://www.uwa.edu.au/projects/data-science-at-uwa", "status": 200, "method": "http", "fetched": "2026-10-29", "text": "Data Science at UWA : The University of Western Australia\nSkip to main content\nAll UWA\nThe University of Western Australia\nShaping the next generation of global leaders.\nStudy\nExplore courses\nDiscover UWA\nHow to apply\nScholarships and fees\nSupport information\nLife at UWA\nAccommodation\nArts and culture\nClubs and societies\nSport and fitness\nStudent Guild\nStudy abroad\nPartners and community\nIndustry partnerships\nCommunity engagement\nGlobal engagement\nOur alumni\nConvocation\nGiving\nOur research\nResearch strengths\nReputation and governance\nResearch degrees\nInstitutes and centres\nInfrastructure\nConnect\nAbout us\nOur history\nReputation\nLeadership and governance\nOur campus\nCampus services\nSchools\nWorking at UWA\nContact us\nCurrent students\nStaff\nLibrary\nNews\nGiving\nEvents\nMenu\nSearch\nHow can we help you?\nClear\nSearch\nThe University of Western Australia\n404\nCallista \u2013 security vulnerability\nEmployee Remediation\nForms\nForms\nRequest academic documents\nThank you\nRule Waiver Form\nThank you\nUWA India\nOpen Day\nSystem Maintenance\nStudy\nStudy\nExplore courses\nFind a course\nStudy areas\nUndergraduate courses\nPostgraduate courses\nHigher Degree by Research\nAssured Pathways\nShort courses\nOur courses explained\nDiscover UWA\nCareer opportunities\nSeek Wisdom\nOur campus\nUWA Albany\nAccommodation\nOpen Day\nEvents\nStudent Exchange and Study Abroad\nHow to apply\nUndergraduate applicants\nPostgraduate applicants\nResearch applicants\nInternational applicants\nPathways and eligibility\nAccept your offer\nDefer your offer\nScholarships and fees\nCalculate your fees\nScholarships\nInternational student fees\nDomestic student fees\nSupport information\nContacts and enquiries\nInternational students\nIndigenous students\nRegional students\nParents and guardians\nHigh schools and career advisors\nAccessibility\nLife at UWA\nLife at UWA\nAccommodation\nArts and culture\nClubs and societies\nSport and fitness\nStudent Guild\nStudy abroad\nDisclaimer and copyright\nPrivacy\nPrivacy\nFAQs\nContact us\nContact us\nMedia\nSubscribe\nThank you\nGraduate career-ready\nMenu\nUWA\nData Science at UWA\nData Science at UWA\nResearch Clusters\nResearch Specialisations\nSchool\nContact\nLeading interdisciplinary research and teaching in the world of Data Science\nData Science at UWA is a major inter-disciplinary research effort that brings together a wide range of world leading experts and top research students already pushing the boundaries in extracting knowledge from data.\nWe have multi-disciplinary groups developing and applying the latest techniques in Data Science, Machine Learning, Artificial Intelligence, Data Management, Analytics, Optimisation and Applied Statistics, to real-world problems in Science, Engineering, Business, Medicine and the Humanities.\nOver 50 researchers are already involved.\nOur research covers the underlying foundational techniques as well as applications. We have teams in computer vision, machine learning development, new techniques in AI, Data gathering via sensors, Data management, Analysis and Optimisation.\nWe deal with data in the form of measurements, text, images, video, audio and multi-media. Data comes from sensors, cameras, automatic transcripts, online and heterogenous sources.\nApplications come from across Engineering, Physical Science, Biological Science, Medicine, Health, Business, Finance, Transport, and Society. Just a few of the current projects include short-term prediction of ocean wave behaviour, traffic congestion, optimisation of maintenance scheduling in mining supply chains, automation of measuring antibiotic effects, wildlife monitoring, detecting leaks in water supply infrastructure, \u2026See the links to the research groups below.\nMost projects involve collaboration with open of our industry partners or a specialised scientific lab.\nResearch student projects are available across the applications and fundamental techniques of data science.\nThe University also offers an innovative Masters Course Program in Data Science, attracting an increasing numbers of students. Many students are already working in industry. The course offers the opportunity to undertake a challenging individual research project with supervisors from CS or Statistics, and co-supervisors from Industry, Science or another application area.\nResearch Clusters\nComplex Data Analysis\nUsing innovative techniques, the Complex Data Modelling research group develop mathematical, statistical and computational methodology to support engineering projects.\nRead more\nResearch Specialisations\nArtificial Intelligence (A.I)\nMachine Learning\nDeep Learning\nIntelligent Systems\nData Analytics\nData Management\nComputer Vision\nResearch opportunities are available for prospective undergraduate, Masters and Doctor of Philosophy students. To submit an expression of interest for a research opportunity, fill out our form or email us.\nSchool of Physics, Mathematics and Computing\nThe School of Physics, Mathematics and Computing gives students a broad education to develop skills to tackle the fast-paced changes in today's world.\nOur courses equip you with practical and theoretical expertise to develop effective and efficient analysis, visualisation, interpretation and technological skills.\nFind out more\nContact Associate Professor Mark Reynolds\nHead of School - Physics, Mathematics and Computing\nPhone\nGet in touch\nEmail\nSend an enquiry\n[email protected]\nClose\nBack to top\nThe University of Western Australia\n35 Stirling Highway\nPerth WA 6009 Australia\n(+61 8) 6488 6000\nEmergency\n(+61 8) 6488 2222\nCRICOS 00126G | PRV12169, Australian University\nAccessibility\nJobs\nStaff portal\nAsk UWA\nPrivacy\nTerms of use\nAustralia\n\u4e2d\u6587\nThe University of Western Australia acknowledges all the Traditional Owners of lands across Australia, including the Whadjuk Noongar people at the Boorloo (Perth) campus and the Menang Noongar people at the Kinjarling (Albany) campus. We recognise and celebrate that Traditional Owners remain the cultural custodians of their lands, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs, and knowledge.\nOriginal illustration by Artist Dr Richard Barry Walley OAM\nIndigenous Portfolio\nThis page\nUpdated\nWednesday, 27 November 2024 12:43 PM (this date excludes nested assets)\nContent ID\nd00b5bca-7738-4633-b66a-33925c494255", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://www.uwa.edu.au/projects/data-science-at-uwa#main-content"], ["", "https://www.uwa.edu.au/"], ["The University of Western Australia", "https://www.uwa.edu.au/"], ["Study", "https://www.uwa.edu.au/study"], ["Explore courses", "https://www.uwa.edu.au/study/explore-courses"], ["Discover UWA", "https://www.uwa.edu.au/study/discover-uwa"], ["How to apply", "https://www.uwa.edu.au/study/how-to-apply"], ["Scholarships and fees", "https://www.uwa.edu.au/study/scholarships-and-fees"], ["Support information", "https://www.uwa.edu.au/study/support-information"], ["Life at UWA", "https://www.uwa.edu.au/life-at-uwa"], ["Accommodation", "https://www.uwa.edu.au/life-at-uwa/accommodation"], ["Arts and culture", "https://www.uwa.edu.au/life-at-uwa/arts-and-culture"], ["Clubs and societies", "https://www.uwa.edu.au/life-at-uwa/clubs-and-societies"], ["Sport and fitness", "https://www.uwa.edu.au/life-at-uwa/sport-and-fitness"], ["Student Guild", "https://www.uwa.edu.au/life-at-uwa/student-guild"], ["Study abroad", "https://www.uwa.edu.au/life-at-uwa/study-abroad"], ["Partners and community", "https://www.uwa.edu.au/partners-and-community"], ["Industry partnerships", "https://www.uwa.edu.au/partners-and-community/partnerships"], ["Community engagement", "https://www.uwa.edu.au/partners-and-community/community-engagem